        <mxCell id="KEhqj0kS6PCCPFDu_pYE-77" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 22px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Figure 1: Hierarchy of existing SRKW information representations.&lt;/b&gt; The 3 data sources capture complementary aspects&lt;/span&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;of SRKW identity, relationships, and observations, with different levels of granularity and identification information.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;[1] Center for Whale Research (CWR) Identification Guide. [2] Dryad Observation Dataset. [3] Whale Museum Sighting Records.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
